# .actrc — local GitHub Actions runner config for `act`
# (https://github.com/nektos/act). Checked in so every clone behaves the same.
#
# Each flag and why it exists:
# -P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
#   Maps the `ubuntu-latest` runner label used by all workflows in
#   .github/workflows/ to act's full Ubuntu image (git, curl, node, docker
#   CLI preinstalled). Without this, act falls back to a micro image that
#   cannot run actions/setup-go / setup-python / setup-uv.
#
# NOTE: `--container-architecture linux/amd64` is intentionally NOT set.
# Add it only if `act` fails on an ARM64 host with an exec-format / image
# platform error; on linux/amd64 hosts it is unnecessary.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
